From 6622c7327d43a7e32043834bb8ea60b5a10846d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:50:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure SHA256 implementation and hardware entropy
 startup

Keep cryptographic initialization, CPU detection, architecture guards and
Info text unchanged. Copy the local SHA256 implementation label before
its scope ends; give existing RdSeed/RdRand notices stable event names.
No random values, seeds or key material are logged.

An actual-node startup fixture checks the buffered implementation label
and exact text after shutdown, including its original local-string
lifetime. Optional hardware notices are checked only when present;
x86 hardware entropy branches are not forced or executed on macOS arm64.
Tier: shared eCash. This does not change V2's primary hash choice.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py==0.51.0; from the commit's parent):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/crypto-startup-diagnostics.json --apply

git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/kernel/context.cpp src/random.cpp

Handwritten: focused functional fixture. Appended public algorithm-label
field is an explicit reviewed support adjustment; existing IDs unchanged.
---
